leable message timestamp footers (#3662)\n\nAdded a `/timestamps` toggle for message timestamp footers in\n`deepagents-code`.\n\n_Opened collaboratively by Mason Daugherty and open-swe._\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <61371264+mdrxy@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"514b8845ecd8f8dafeebcc905c3a651942d9a19e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/514b8845ecd8f8dafeebcc905c3a651942d9a19e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/977e11006cfbd78fbaba4e7bb2a13acf6b788652","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGmUNCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAowcQAFGWW/USosc0LgpyB+j+9T+3\nUVyTGsS0oRPESFnayA7K1g+oFS+FQ/H795AWTx70FZ9BsBC2TN+PIqlug9e2ieRk\nN5evQgMeDbbuhLitLCC/ThlZJDHRHGvHih3CvPjKGWmhFGmyU2/58hb1l8DAwdHz\n/ru7aDT1Zd8/lK5AXDN7vtHSFeUpy5wfDbVL1wTYW/EJQNCyUQMF+Xc0JzCUrZIz\n3038Pmz0PfOHxQlPxzmBB2QjjQhmJPvQdkNkj6jFquvs2ZzHDoVzU0uQNzsNnlfE\nzUw6uRlX66Xez0GAoeNuYsILkjKDVtvQQSkiI1JZqCFbsM6lZAKqNKFkHDsuOUkP\nRjw1lpy5WzojzImJYcvi+Cjop4Cg4DolFlDMiDAl3HpoxH7QXdApudHS763oNf3J\n25kJDJYiaWAgfnS8bBLoySkPUhvCBFkysCRSQVVuUpc3tqzivc3ZgDIaRbYsao7r\nqycGRoshAZCjXTb4dCinXSu1L0RdduLc7b/GBpMZZo+XYE3mBq7KKfzfPbTQajul\n5A6z2zhdS28qPtIeP1YutYHHG5KWF7UjieA9d5+fsqh1tw5STjk3QmjQJh3pLLoJ\nH5zntGiybz+PLP6RD9Je42BRhN8gSoVTksofE9XF7B09G+dGQdU5n5LXfdJHZRcl\nkpsozQvikbiHU2OG4neO\n=ERil\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 514b8845ecd8f8dafeebcc905c3a651942d9a19e\nparent 9857a08b6144b2f001d8f4bf03ac2f254c6b2da4\nauthor open-swe[bot] <215916821+open-swe[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1780114701 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780114701 +0000\n\nfeat(code): add toggleable message timestamp footers (#3662)\n\nAdded a `/timestamps` toggle for message timestamp footers in\n`deepagents-code`.\n\n_Opened collaboratively by Mason Daugherty and open-swe._\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: open-swe[bot] <open-swe@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <61371264+mdrxy@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-05-30T04:18:22Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/977e11006cfbd78fbaba4e7bb2a13acf6b788652","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/977e11006cfbd78fbaba4e7bb2a13acf6b788652","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/977e11006cfbd78fbaba4e7bb2a13acf6b788652/comments","author":{"login":"open-swe[bot]","id":215916821,"node_id":"BOT_kgDODN6hFQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1395372?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/open-swe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/open-swe%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"9857a08b6144b2f001d8f4bf03ac2f254c6b2da4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9857a08b6144b2f001d8f4bf03ac2f254c6b2da4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9857a08b6144b2f001d8f4bf03ac2f254c6b2da4"}]},{"sha":"9857a08b6144b2f001d8f4bf03ac2f254c6b2da4","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDk4NTdhMDhiNjE0NGIyZjAwMWQ4ZjRiZjAzYWMyZjI1NGM2YjJkYTQ","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-05-30T00:50:52Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-30T00:50:52Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): handle base64 reads with unknown file extensions (#3663)\n\nCloses #3657\n\n---\n\nBinary file reads now respect the backend-declared `encoding` before\ndeciding whether content should be line-numbered as text. This prevents\nbase64 payloads for extensions outside the multimodal block map, like\n`.docx`, from being treated as plain text.\n\n## Changes\n- Route `FilesystemMiddleware` read results with `encoding=\"base64\"`\nthrough binary `content_blocks` even when `_get_file_type` returns\n`text`.\n- Fall back to a generic `file` block for unknown binary extensions\nwhile still using `mimetypes.guess_type` to preserve the best available\nmedia type.\n- Keep existing image/audio/video handling unchanged by using the mapped\nblock type whenever the extension is recognized.","tree":{"sha":"839288944e056a23982c674ea5ac425e7f90c04e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/839288944e056a23982c674ea5ac425e7f90c04e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/9857a08b6144b2f001d8f4bf03ac2f254c6b2da4","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGjRsCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAC4QADpHx6uC+J8osRuyyasoW9WG\nqCqq5UwOYc16yEx6hduLb5Y8vzulogFH6N5Gzsp+9T36lDsHCtUa8il3ToFuxPMk\nXttejwUi62k4VgVg0WdnrGUORyfYIAE6XRoUGq9pVYjCTg9JJYpspRLRdEf3aJKC\n5ME7tbBH+ClQfhWOGu6EygmKBkvmiTWRamHFicf9DMuBIhp0mH3OUXKf+BmpGZ5t\nP9LXoHmEdw9qMrXJxsgUEv/hu5kIwV/BzqTVnDb9Szn93IAL8CTKbmruLDWNbtdQ\n8YSRvBnsllRkPZoLExc3fSbGmgSY4K+pFWvGMXG75JqVmh6Ys0YbJXLNwdZEB/rD\n0HTGYQbPcchea7vAygTgZP86rKwUk13vTVXVOe8sy5AAZeCv4ZevYQfHLT3GfMuE\n1PS0px+lvb8Pb3yMYkMSGYn90+pnw1dcX3D9BVko5ZqV1YrgT12/oXUC3E5XLlaK\nlOXi9C69hUVFgsKnHEFeSsbbl3RgSvHVI15XiRCpsj16cUrTID9d0Lyd5/77sKQ2\nW0txE62WEdX4dddUmOa5NF5Ggj3ARdYuSceQc8us98g6bdEoXZ8dGu9BDs1fWo40\nagphiEtJ7Vo1MiWUgG83F37fTYbX82NUQDmQbNaEML1sRYmSObT6d0i7AKmuZI4F\n9FixnKSBC4fOneVFHiz5\n=enMX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 839288944e056a23982c674ea5ac425e7f90c04e\nparent 54485a305854f46a6ce00ae4df51f3301c652a38\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1780102252 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780102252 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): handle base64 reads with unknown file extensions (#3663)\n\nCloses #3657\n\n---\n\nBinary file reads now respect the backend-declared `encoding` before\ndeciding whether content should be line-numbered as text. This prevents\nbase64 payloads for extensions outside the multimodal block map, like\n`.docx`, from being treated as plain text.\n\n## Changes\n- Route `FilesystemMiddleware` read results with `encoding=\"base64\"`\nthrough binary `content_blocks` even when `_get_file_type` returns\n`text`.\n- Fall back to a generic `file` block for unknown binary extensions\nwhile still using `mimetypes.guess_type` to preserve the best available\nmedia type.\n- Keep existing image/audio/video handling unchanged by using the mapped\nblock type whenever the extension is recognized.","verified_at":"2026-05-30T00:50:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9857a08b6144b2f001d8f4bf03ac2f254c6b2da4","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/9857a08b6144b2f001d8f4bf03ac2f254c6b2da4","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/9857a08b6144b2f001d8f4bf03ac2f254c6b2da4/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"54485a305854f46a6ce00ae4df51f3301c652a38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/54485a305854f46a6ce00ae4df51f3301c652a38","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/54485a305854f46a6ce00ae4df51f3301c652a38"}]},{"sha":"54485a305854f46a6ce00ae4df51f3301c652a38","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDU0NDg1YTMwNTg1NGY0NmE2Y2UwMGFlNGRmNTFmMzMwMWM2NTJhMzg","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-05-29T22:54:01Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-29T22:54:01Z"},"message":"fix(code): tool spinner, result formatting, and expand-hint fixes (#3661)\n\nSeveral display fixes for the TUI, centered on auto-executed read tools\n(`grep`, `glob`, `read_file`, `ls`). Previously these sat idle with no\nspinner until results arrived, scoped searches were indistinguishable in\nthe transcript, and the expand/collapse hint frequently promised an\nexpansion that revealed nothing.\n\n## Changes\n- Show a per-tool running spinner the moment an auto-executed tool\nmounts, instead of falling back to the global \"Thinking\" spinner. Tools\nthat then block on HITL approval or `ask_user` are paused via a new\n`ToolCallMessage.pause_running`, which reverts the row to its pending\nlook and resets the elapsed timer so it doesn't misleadingly read\n\"Running…\"; the approve branches call `set_running` to resume.\n- Append the scoped `path` to `grep`/`glob` displays when it's\nnon-default via `_format_scope_path` in `tool_display.py` — the glob\ndefault (`\"/\"`) and grep default (`None`) are omitted, so two\notherwise-identical calls on different directories are now\ndistinguishable.\n- Compact `read_file`'s `cat -n` gutter for display via\n`ToolCallMessage._compact_line_gutter`: line numbers are right-justified\nto the widest number present plus two spaces, replacing the raw\n6-wide-plus-tab format, while preserving source indentation and passing\nnon-numbered lines through untouched.\n- Fix the expand/collapse affordance so it only appears when the\nformatter actually hides content. The raw size threshold alone could\ntrip on long single-line `grep`/`glob` output that truncates by line\ncount, and force-expanded errors have no smaller collapsed form — both\ncases previously showed a misleading hint. `_has_expandable_output` now\ngates this in both directions.\n- Drop the leading four-space indent from `glob`/`grep` result lines so\nthey sit flush left.","tree":{"sha":"1263e0f533200c5e2b40f72e239679836ba43af0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/1263e0f533200c5e2b40f72e239679836ba43af0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/54485a305854f46a6ce00ae4df51f3301c652a38","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGhkJCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKvsQAE1VXDin7EIC7YLNjcVjPCiW\nyJ6LJIx+ILXaXRkrAafJmU85MmxF18/70hIOknC0qDVod2tolwNQxONlvNr1VM8T\nwTP0yc/qTRFS/cG0dJ467fXlYFTJndCFu/0H0KreuSbjTqFf1p8MBZIA6hR6BwXQ\nV1eZxaBnUZRQPNjEYy/Z1g9Klm0Epz+p7rVPfDZ0g7XPtpn2ZdBZMx/K3yodI+BP\nM+L7GApu3tN/xdUehJ+m0JSbzAT8MHWUzeXSinNjxr/GhpqqF/dU+LEaZgoc6PyP\n4OY+yoK9dhipYv+WYcOlfx+8CxuKmvXKYQeDPXUdn4+xaL5LXdHxzV0Ocv1FMKtn\nMx14nU36dnbYgzuSS92BBXgCJTrKGfy/OERsHDG1VhzU/u8vgUuW1qTx39jIx7zo\nKcIotvh4/1/Wz2cWgw9CLHgR0rh7YbKUGDu/wnXl7Xl3wWkhB4z9RVPokuvtFxSo\nw19hx7xtLq+u76uGTfc38W8wk7o9aUHX1EoyqMUpYFGx6jpH9Qll40BlTPdt7i2J\n2pBTgU8a+0YG5fdSJKWse11S464XTo8dUDh8Fzy6v0D63LcTA6/HPhMjAqB01Ia4\n1e4EZ1VyN3Fdj+YTMKpsEhwaSriOCqrV+FVJZ2CDpbaX+KtEoKR2WowrC+zNNwn6\nYxlsnV5rLmGWPQb+3HlL\n=8RIx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 1263e0f533200c5e2b40f72e239679836ba43af0\nparent d92aef68f70a5e5277c43a50581e7895e682c417\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1780095241 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780095241 -0400\n\nfix(code): tool spinner, result formatting, and expand-hint fixes (#3661)\n\nSeveral display fixes for the TUI, centered on auto-executed read tools\n(`grep`, `glob`, `read_file`, `ls`). Previously these sat idle with no\nspinner until results arrived, scoped searches were indistinguishable in\nthe transcript, and the expand/collapse hint frequently promised an\nexpansion that revealed nothing.\n\n## Changes\n- Show a per-tool running spinner the moment an auto-executed tool\nmounts, instead of falling back to the global \"Thinking\" spinner. Tools\nthat then block on HITL approval or `ask_user` are paused via a new\n`ToolCallMessage.pause_running`, which reverts the row to its pending\nlook and resets the elapsed timer so it doesn't misleadingly read\n\"Running…\"; the approve branches call `set_running` to resume.\n- Append the scoped `path` to `grep`/`glob` displays when it's\nnon-default via `_format_scope_path` in `tool_display.py` — the glob\ndefault (`\"/\"`) and grep default (`None`) are omitted, so two\notherwise-identical calls on different directories are now\ndistinguishable.\n- Compact `read_file`'s `cat -n` gutter for display via\n`ToolCallMessage._compact_line_gutter`: line numbers are right-justified\nto the widest number present plus two spaces, replacing the raw\n6-wide-plus-tab format, while preserving source indentation and passing\nnon-numbered lines through untouched.\n- Fix the expand/collapse affordance so it only appears when the\nformatter actually hides content. The raw size threshold alone could\ntrip on long single-line `grep`/`glob` output that truncates by line\ncount, and force-expanded errors have no smaller collapsed form — both\ncases previously showed a misleading hint. `_has_expandable_output` now\ngates this in both directions.\n- Drop the leading four-space indent from `glob`/`grep` result lines so\nthey sit flush left.","verified_at":"2026-05-29T22:54:02Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/54485a305854f46a6ce00ae4df51f3301c652a38","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/54485a305854f46a6ce00ae4df51f3301c652a38","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/54485a305854f46a6ce00ae4df51f3301c652a38/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_