024` across\nrelease-please-managed CHANGELOGs where duplicate `### Features`/`###\nBug Fixes` headings are unavoidable.","tree":{"sha":"76aa9c3950988985811da91dfd951186cd9f51c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/76aa9c3950988985811da91dfd951186cd9f51c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/bda376124c8f24c6a6c813c96eda5f63a5ca41d1","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGFzwCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAVWQQAAo2L4V8ewndcCLGc9KfYBh1\nzBYpHWR0fdlWo1WBLBLNvSTdHKuIfz+EiVMhm5ejL/pgxSe6Hna+DAy99cRVGE+3\nBfnR6o1/SqNq87BJwATkEwm6GZCzBfGPY4eit0Nvt7FsXtpsWzqQTB3IqXTUCt2L\naYri52RWQdBInzU/HGusSpuTG7+HTkPlH/EA0Nex0//rX7CjJQuCf2qMZdbgVFET\neULbFEl03N93yuWksPYXGmYnidpPt73URLCd3nCQ8iQ6zfNpUC9FvZ+vDVVPDXI6\nOvdFtLaasobQgXMGjOhrRmr+ZCvsJsEQ64hI5vWSuLKs8o34riZzJEQSANW8gzcp\nEEp6uEN1qbWpKGEordVeuzmM6yNVsLcQhF22qYRfuO4Kp/yooHeQtupuoxs9aSVt\n9Q8dI0tAI40m/Om7fA9n7vciINRFhsK0muzOtxXMD8vzYqxXjUMfrlVcN58P+KtG\npog7/WU+7h+f/QenaM1An2DVqUpeV8TGfcClU5UqjIi7QdqiG+QA6k4oZRhaah8e\nXyadBrdYHXGgFHFDqcWa7fQxkd/bNNcneP4zrc3h3Ulzn1oY47A/0yNZGnTmee1q\nUTjo6juwZwJbW1x2286DWu6MzbcG79vvNVaEuZeVXabMfdgt54sSEb9Lqoq4Nufu\n8Au7Zy7+HL09JZgzfHqW\n=rFX2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 76aa9c3950988985811da91dfd951186cd9f51c4\nparent 2abc33081daf9f23a105b3a170ab7f4e92d2288c\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1779981551 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779981551 -0400\n\nchore(infra): tighten commit lint and silence changelog markdownlint (#3643)\n\nAdds a local commit-message hook so Conventional Commits violations are\ncaught before push, and clarifies the CI error when a PR title has\nsurrounding whitespace. Also silences `MD024` across\nrelease-please-managed CHANGELOGs where duplicate `### Features`/`###\nBug Fixes` headings are unavoidable.","verified_at":"2026-05-28T15:19:13Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bda376124c8f24c6a6c813c96eda5f63a5ca41d1","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/bda376124c8f24c6a6c813c96eda5f63a5ca41d1","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/bda376124c8f24c6a6c813c96eda5f63a5ca41d1/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"2abc33081daf9f23a105b3a170ab7f4e92d2288c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2abc33081daf9f23a105b3a170ab7f4e92d2288c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2abc33081daf9f23a105b3a170ab7f4e92d2288c"}]},{"sha":"2abc33081daf9f23a105b3a170ab7f4e92d2288c","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDJhYmMzMzA4MWRhZjlmMjNhMTA1YjNhMTcwYWI3ZjRlOTJkMjI4OGM","commit":{"author":{"name":"github-actions[bot]","email":"41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-05-28T15:09:17Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T15:09:17Z"},"message":"release(deepagents): 0.6.5 (#3602)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.6.5](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents==0.6.4...deepagents==0.6.5)\n(2026-05-28)\n\n### Features\n\n* `RubricMiddleware` for self-evaluated agent iteration\n([#3529](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3529))\n([5b8d44d](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5b8d44d65c6ec43084687019cf00a37d730ac2fa))\n* Log when grep falls back from ripgrep\n([#3593](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3593))\n([379b1ff](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/379b1ffdc3ccf5da72d9f7264d531be108f0b36d))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Use `file_path` kwarg in `read_file` examples\n([#3630](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3630))\n([97946ee](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/97946ee09eb167c63d8c07f8bb116f40cfc9603f))\n* `read_file` pagination skipping lines after wrapping\n([#3641](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3641))\n([390551d](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/390551d61d57ce68c2a80ed78c07eaa8e985908b))\n* Handle `None` state in messages delta reducer\n([#3636](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3636))\n([5a6d920](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5a6d920d9dec2199cbe743062a5cc1ff8f298567))\n* Return grep errors for sandbox exec failures\n([#3637](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3637))\n([f87d61f](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f87d61f01a23fcfb994e88b7f9324d404e66faef))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","tree":{"sha":"9256e45ca9281423c202f059552675d54c60912e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/9256e45ca9281423c202f059552675d54c60912e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/2abc33081daf9f23a105b3a170ab7f4e92d2288c","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGFqdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAe8sQAGwr6Zjq9AaixUCVoLfQ6Txy\ne5dPYgDZ+LTHh2lpJkD9TLD5ig+WdGwyqyVCApzzMX3GBZh2ByedbrLBrxo7L2Z/\nhBtX+0DlttfwOimF8q9ewJxfGMRkI0l8+SmryBE1Wj3PuZtAaXqjRTVRP8AytPG2\nHngGci5XBKW+mak1CVZa9R57tt6P4ZqlCT3GxojQvXwKvUO5k22Ddkhd0Qh0qZDO\nBVV0swAlV08gdpWC6wrJViCkOqJRWw6CzCszMYEMO1ArnedHN/MKAF222gulzuQG\nE3fh+w8HQMeOQ4xMTHdbRuKXDA64vv+FZefla5zUFiUV9+vfmUzctvJxinmuJXIk\nuj+Lw1dPuWsHyoSMYTlzTaZ/GwPWN984GoCBx9gqp6Y/07+mXB/pKAklNv1aQlbJ\nSteDnXcvrDJI5cBdEQ6R/W29dPjGDVaTYXInlkH72i/bFcKm2h1UBzuogLzYUUMb\nnTmYRA8kymvMAhqqlsz1c+eB/gi7WZXb1TzPVTRcI7UN0UoB439awUcSxOiP6HXx\nT7i9fb5+kufgbz45Qae2P0DP6kuSKd7Tgdo77gSeeX20wtUctNoyFN6tC0Jbq4/D\nH6KPceTeBA/Q0c6zob63VqDGQM7xHbAg0QRoKYz32sZ3FxUuPu2LCUCe73C9I6LT\nBltisKL9w3G37L2FVaz3\n=94Qv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 9256e45ca9281423c202f059552675d54c60912e\nparent 5b8d44d65c6ec43084687019cf00a37d730ac2fa\nauthor github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com> 1779980957 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779980957 -0400\n\nrelease(deepagents): 0.6.5 (#3602)\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Merging this PR will automatically publish to **PyPI** and create a\n**GitHub release**.\n\nFor the full release process, see\n[`.github/RELEASING.md`](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md).\n\n---\n\n_Everything below this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n\n##\n[0.6.5](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/compare/deepagents==0.6.4...deepagents==0.6.5)\n(2026-05-28)\n\n### Features\n\n* `RubricMiddleware` for self-evaluated agent iteration\n([#3529](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3529))\n([5b8d44d](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5b8d44d65c6ec43084687019cf00a37d730ac2fa))\n* Log when grep falls back from ripgrep\n([#3593](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3593))\n([379b1ff](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/379b1ffdc3ccf5da72d9f7264d531be108f0b36d))\n\n### Bug Fixes\n\n* Use `file_path` kwarg in `read_file` examples\n([#3630](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3630))\n([97946ee](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/97946ee09eb167c63d8c07f8bb116f40cfc9603f))\n* `read_file` pagination skipping lines after wrapping\n([#3641](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3641))\n([390551d](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/390551d61d57ce68c2a80ed78c07eaa8e985908b))\n* Handle `None` state in messages delta reducer\n([#3636](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3636))\n([5a6d920](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5a6d920d9dec2199cbe743062a5cc1ff8f298567))\n* Return grep errors for sandbox exec failures\n([#3637](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/issues/3637))\n([f87d61f](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f87d61f01a23fcfb994e88b7f9324d404e66faef))\n\n---\n\n_Everything above this line will be the GitHub release body._\n\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> A **New Contributors** section is appended to the GitHub release notes\nautomatically at publish time (see [Release\nPipeline](https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/blob/main/.github/RELEASING.md#release-pipeline),\nstep 2).\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: github-actions[bot] <41898282+github-actions[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T15:09:39Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2abc33081daf9f23a105b3a170ab7f4e92d2288c","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/2abc33081daf9f23a105b3a170ab7f4e92d2288c","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/2abc33081daf9f23a105b3a170ab7f4e92d2288c/comments","author":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5b8d44d65c6ec43084687019cf00a37d730ac2fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5b8d44d65c6ec43084687019cf00a37d730ac2fa","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5b8d44d65c6ec43084687019cf00a37d730ac2fa"}]},{"sha":"5b8d44d65c6ec43084687019cf00a37d730ac2fa","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDViOGQ0NGQ2NWM2ZWM0MzA4NDY4NzAxOWNmMDBhMzdkNzMwYWMyZmE","commit":{"author":{"name":"Shrikar Seshadri","email":"146694785+davibinboi@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-05-28T14:58:26Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-28T14:58:26Z"},"message":"feat(sdk): `RubricMiddleware` for self-evaluated agent iteration (#3529)\n\n### Fixes:\nAdds RubricMiddleware, which lets a caller declare what correct outputs\nlook like via a rubric supplied on state.\n\nAfter the agent completes an iteration and has what it thinks is a\nresult, a separate grader sub-agent spins up, evaluates the transcript,\nand determines if further revision is needed. If so, the main agent is\nlooped again with the grader's feedback on what in the rubric's criteria\nwas not satisfactory (synthetic HumanMessage tagged with\nname=\"rubric_grader\"). The loop terminates on satisfied,\nmax_iterations_reached, or grader failed. KeyboardInterrupt and\nasyncio.CancelledError propagate so Ctrl+C / cancellation are preserved.\n\n### Usage:\n\n```python\nfrom deepagents import create_deep_agent\nfrom deepagents.middleware.outcomes import RubricMiddleware\n\nagent = create_deep_agent(\n    model=\"anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n    middleware=[\n        RubricMiddleware(\n            model=\"anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n            system_prompt=\"You are a strict grader. Only mark satisfied when every criterion is verifiable from the transcript.\",\n            max_iterations=3,\n        )\n    ],\n)\n```\n\nRubricMiddleware takes flat kwargs:\n\n- model (required): the grader's model. Accepts a \"provider:model-id\"\nstring or a BaseChatModel instance.\n- system_prompt (optional): replaces the built-in grader prompt.\n- tools (optional): tools the grader may call before verdicting (e.g.\ncount_words, a test runner). Defaults to no tools (pure-LLM grader).\n- max_iterations (optional, default 3, hard-capped at 20): grader\niterations per rubric attempt before terminating with\nmax_iterations_reached.\n- on_evaluation (optional): callback invoked with each RubricEvaluation.\n\nThe rubric itself is supplied per-invocation on state ({\"rubric\":\n\"...\"}) and is sticky across follow-up turns on the same thread.\n\n### What's included:\n\n**`RubricMiddleware` core** —\n`libs/deepagents/deepagents/middleware/outcomes.py`\nThe middleware itself, plus all public types: `RubricResult`,\n`RubricState`, `RubricEvaluation`, `CriterionEval`, `GraderResponse`,\nand the `RUBRIC_GRADER_MESSAGE_SOURCE` tag.\n\n**Re-exports**:\n· `deepagents/__init__.py` (just the middleware) \n· `deepagents/middleware/__init__.py` (middleware + public types)\n\n---\n\n**Unit tests** — `tests/unit_tests/middleware/test_rubric_middleware.py`\n\nCovers construction validation, `before_agent` rubric-change detection,\ngrader plumbing (lazy construction, model/prompt/tools propagation,\nnonce-bracketed prompt-injection hardening), transcript shaping, and\nmulti-invocation rubric stickiness.\n\n**End-to-end tests** —\n`tests/unit_tests/test_end_to_end.py::TestRubricMiddlewareEndToEnd`\n\nDrives a real `create_deep_agent` with fake chat models for both main\nand grader agents. Exercises all four terminal statuses (`satisfied`,\n`needs_revision → satisfied`, `max_iterations_reached`, `grader\nexception → failed`), synthetic-message tagging, `KeyboardInterrupt`\npropagation, and custom system prompt honoring.\n\n---\n\n**Evals** —\n`libs/evals/tests/evals/test_iterative_constraint_satisfaction.py` ·\n`EVAL_CATALOG.md` · `utils.py`\n\nTests whether a model with RubricMiddleware can hit an exact word count\nwhile starting every sentence with a custom phrase. Uses a deterministic\ngrader to verify the middleware's verdict matches ground truth.\n\n\n### Breaking changes:\n\nNone - this middleware is a no-op until a rubric is supplied on state,\nso it's safe to install unconditionally.\n\n### How I verified my code:\n\n- make format, make lint, make test from libs/deepagents/\n- TestRubricMiddlewareEndToEnd drives all four terminal statuses under a\nreal create_deep_agent stack.\n- Iterative-constraint-satisfaction eval runs against claude-sonnet-4-6\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","tree":{"sha":"d41baa4be58595a206e045331a7d646b49e97a56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/d41baa4be58595a206e045331a7d646b49e97a56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5b8d44d65c6ec43084687019cf00a37d730ac2fa","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqGFgSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAqAQAHciddaOdbgJAHDZ6TA1eDdK\nuIlkX2cbzisrO88/T3U2r3Iek3NpOPn1gSqGiE1f/I7Yi2RbhB3KFt/v/DjImOQn\ndoaSLSTydm69UE0Xi1EDmSILdu212nOV3qrzyiDYaugyk2PDzbaVpHJFR0ExzWwZ\nYhR/Erg18CvLqlJDTFoFWSyrzwHMD7c/JOXHw/C6+NSdEKTIkpLWT0QrrFkizShL\nEFaWvfaSCfdmfokehCOcZAGRu6OUk/G9YP25GDhhYRwPs0VoNOCKUUuRtACP1FYn\n6E8fI0EvsTBFm+9nwXFxv/kg6Nmc9xfzdH3FmwBo4PIUeQ3lEG08YchFzDbpKBjy\nyQZ6jo6puTUlykf8bNT68Nwrpr8KKZoGLHfBfszuZPKeMe+W9HVEGD1yevKF94e+\nFiORafVgbR0ZNeU0RH4EQu0RpBjzpypDK+25BXM18hGxYnCHHKVxUE3QXEFE/VhM\nthkU7tzwOup42w5tr9kHUWs8T+pL0gU+CFInyNT/1qW0Csy9D33wUZ5W0D6NJr2v\nnlcmNAxzuIs08LjDNxIPb9zC8aa1oJnILkcGCNMcmnwgMsgiZoFdLc+kSzub1B7F\nY1CEDkkkWY2ZdtLARbxUKOJ2jo4NZ4wgH8nPJRtCdWTDvFmsouJLrjGSuCEReIye\nzOFjx3Df8s3VVheSsf+e\n=7Hs6\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree d41baa4be58595a206e045331a7d646b49e97a56\nparent 390551d61d57ce68c2a80ed78c07eaa8e985908b\nauthor Shrikar Seshadri <146694785+davibinboi@users.noreply.github.com> 1779980306 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779980306 -0400\n\nfeat(sdk): `RubricMiddleware` for self-evaluated agent iteration (#3529)\n\n### Fixes:\nAdds RubricMiddleware, which lets a caller declare what correct outputs\nlook like via a rubric supplied on state.\n\nAfter the agent completes an iteration and has what it thinks is a\nresult, a separate grader sub-agent spins up, evaluates the transcript,\nand determines if further revision is needed. If so, the main agent is\nlooped again with the grader's feedback on what in the rubric's criteria\nwas not satisfactory (synthetic HumanMessage tagged with\nname=\"rubric_grader\"). The loop terminates on satisfied,\nmax_iterations_reached, or grader failed. KeyboardInterrupt and\nasyncio.CancelledError propagate so Ctrl+C / cancellation are preserved.\n\n### Usage:\n\n```python\nfrom deepagents import create_deep_agent\nfrom deepagents.middleware.outcomes import RubricMiddleware\n\nagent = create_deep_agent(\n    model=\"anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n    middleware=[\n        RubricMiddleware(\n            model=\"anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6\",\n            system_prompt=\"You are a strict grader. Only mark satisfied when every criterion is verifiable from the transcript.\",\n            max_iterations=3,\n        )\n    ],\n)\n```\n\nRubricMiddleware takes flat kwargs:\n\n- model (required): the grader's model. Accepts a \"provider:model-id\"\nstring or a BaseChatModel instance.\n- system_prompt (optional): replaces the built-in grader prompt.\n- tools (optional): tools the grader may call before verdicting (e.g.\ncount_words, a test runner). Defaults to no tools (pure-LLM grader).\n- max_iterations (optional, default 3, hard-capped at 20): grader\niterations per rubric attempt before terminating with\nmax_iterations_reached.\n- on_evaluation (optional): callback invoked with each RubricEvaluation.\n\nThe rubric itself is supplied per-invocation on state ({\"rubric\":\n\"...\"}) and is sticky across follow-up turns on the same thread.\n\n### What's included:\n\n**`RubricMiddleware` core** —\n`libs/deepagents/deepagents/middleware/outcomes.py`\nThe middleware itself, plus all public types: `RubricResult`,\n`RubricState`, `RubricEvaluation`, `CriterionEval`, `GraderResponse`,\nand the `RUBRIC_GRADER_MESSAGE_SOURCE` tag.\n\n**Re-exports**:\n· `deepagents/__init__.py` (just the middleware) \n· `deepagents/middleware/__init__.py` (middleware + public types)\n\n---\n\n**Unit tests** — `tests/unit_tests/middleware/test_rubric_middleware.py`\n\nCovers construction validation, `before_agent` rubric-change detection,\ngrader plumbing (lazy construction, model/prompt/tools propagation,\nnonce-bracketed prompt-injection hardening), transcript shaping, and\nmulti-invocation rubric stickiness.\n\n**End-to-end tests** —\n`tests/unit_tests/test_end_to_end.py::TestRubricMiddlewareEndToEnd`\n\nDrives a real `create_deep_agent` with fake chat models for both main\nand grader agents. Exercises all four terminal statuses (`satisfied`,\n`needs_revision → satisfied`, `max_iterations_reached`, `grader\nexception → failed`), synthetic-message tagging, `KeyboardInterrupt`\npropagation, and custom system prompt honoring.\n\n---\n\n**Evals** —\n`libs/evals/tests/evals/test_iterative_constraint_satisfaction.py` ·\n`EVAL_CATALOG.md` · `utils.py`\n\nTests whether a model with RubricMiddleware can hit an exact word count\nwhile starting every sentence with a custom phrase. Uses a deterministic\ngrader to verify the middleware's verdict matches ground truth.\n\n\n### Breaking changes:\n\nNone - this middleware is a no-op until a rubric is supplied on state,\nso it's safe to install unconditionally.\n\n### How I verified my code:\n\n- make format, make lint, make test from libs/deepagents/\n- TestRubricMiddlewareEndToEnd drives all four terminal statuses under a\nreal create_deep_agent stack.\n- Iterative-constraint-satisfaction eval runs against claude-sonnet-4-6\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <github@mdrxy.com>\nCo-authored-by: Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev>","verified_at":"2026-05-28T14:58:27Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5b8d44d65c6ec43084687019cf00a37d730ac2fa","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5b8d44d65c6ec43084687019cf00a37d730ac2fa","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5b8d44d65c6ec43084687019cf00a37d730ac2fa/comments","author":{"login":"davibinboi","id":146694785,"node_id":"U_kgDOCL5igQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146694785?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi","html_url":"https://github.com/davibinboi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/davibinboi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"390551d61d57ce68c2a80ed78c07eaa8e985908b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/390551d61d57ce68c2a80ed78c07eaa8e985908b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/390551d61d57ce68c2a80ed78c07eaa8e985908b"}]},{"sha":"390551d61d57ce68c2a80ed78c07eaa8e985908b","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDM5MDU1MWQ2MWQ1N2NlNjhjMmE4MGVkNzhjMDdlYWE4ZTk4NTkwOGI","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-05-27T21:02:16Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-27T21:02:16Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): `read_file` pagination skipping lines after wrapping (#3641)\n\nCloses #2453\n\n---\n\n`read_file` applies row-based truncation twice: once when the backend\nslices raw lines by `offset`/`limit`, then again after\n`format_content_with_line_numbers` wraps long lines into continuation\nrows. When a wrapped line inflates the row count past `limit`, real\nsource lines fall off the page — and the next page resumes from `offset\n+ limit`, skipping them entirely.\n\n`_truncate` now takes the row-based limit as optional. The new-style\n`ReadResult` path (the backend has already paginated by source lines)\ndrops the row chop and keeps only the byte-budget cap. The legacy `str`\nbackend path keeps the row-based behavior, since those backends still\nformat with line numbers inline.\n\n`limit` now bounds *source* lines, not formatted rows — a wrapped\n15k-char line with `limit=3` renders all of its continuation chunks\nalongside the surrounding source lines instead of silently dropping the\ntail. The `read_file` tool description is updated to match.\n\nCarries forward the fix originally proposed in #2452 by @farrimoh; that\nPR was closed and could not be reopened, so the patch was rewritten\nagainst current `main` with farrimoh credited as a co-author on the\ncommit.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: farrimoh <farri.mohajerani@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"553dee18a1f9d3c83f1913426f7a5fc626f4f1a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/553dee18a1f9d3c83f1913426f7a5fc626f4f1a3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/390551d61d57ce68c2a80ed78c07eaa8e985908b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqF1vZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA5UEQAJexkiFmQmP4aRL9RahEd6GG\nzhjvlkiO3WJcqeBpGgZYRKXtE2NjszE4SReMwNRCja6NwgBt7i1Ax6LPuWzSqPY5\npV9eTPO0RC53onEf0u2w6XgPIeHxvYdrZyWQ5wiTiKvLiv88ClNmgIAVfc9esWnp\njJosVnPGcsT5Wo9m54b9PiFZQRnyKQUhlUurppNCH4ewi+UIGerGnm2KDHS49L3b\nVRklNiWCSAcDak0DaVAFA0qVYqk3oI70qEAu3syyF7g4dvks3P0gFaFhUw5YuNof\nWGfRLmFPnxQ0Nd2qAPnHBZrLhKKDHidRhq9Gv1ZlHfmRrHHqT0tonFCRIVqkg2yN\nDdqcrTR8JPRO14IJ33z8dDtwBOaiWUdpkuuxxrc7hy97YiWjpWReltzB1JXJBupI\n+vMHZgxhkdaG8LWHgPV1VpNqft2Qz92RqzJHmHqem/xCfol8fvU5k1vCaGI8P+gb\nnc0v9540opP8doJeX3vynTmGITi9HQVNlKMrclzqn/fXcjJHrIPwQbMTc6LBEqUj\nF+edWdPlYFoEQuCAVGDmOXVZK56AtgORspMFIw2pyYHLMcfnGeS5QYu5oaLZVk7Q\nigB7rfUGJLWRa437hsGgTwM/0IjqKbQwKNkDnkaSCrwOnX3ILvjN31ax32MEJwDw\nmOnS5a/f5xZbBrM5Ftol\n=zzBe\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 553dee18a1f9d3c83f1913426f7a5fc626f4f1a3\nparent f87d61f01a23fcfb994e88b7f9324d404e66faef\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1779915736 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779915736 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): `read_file` pagination skipping lines after wrapping (#3641)\n\nCloses #2453\n\n---\n\n`read_file` applies row-based truncation twice: once when the backend\nslices raw lines by `offset`/`limit`, then again after\n`format_content_with_line_numbers` wraps long lines into continuation\nrows. When a wrapped line inflates the row count past `limit`, real\nsource lines fall off the page — and the next page resumes from `offset\n+ limit`, skipping them entirely.\n\n`_truncate` now takes the row-based limit as optional. The new-style\n`ReadResult` path (the backend has already paginated by source lines)\ndrops the row chop and keeps only the byte-budget cap. The legacy `str`\nbackend path keeps the row-based behavior, since those backends still\nformat with line numbers inline.\n\n`limit` now bounds *source* lines, not formatted rows — a wrapped\n15k-char line with `limit=3` renders all of its continuation chunks\nalongside the surrounding source lines instead of silently dropping the\ntail. The `read_file` tool description is updated to match.\n\nCarries forward the fix originally proposed in #2452 by @farrimoh; that\nPR was closed and could not be reopened, so the patch was rewritten\nagainst current `main` with farrimoh credited as a co-author on the\ncommit.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: farrimoh <farri.mohajerani@gmail.com>","verified_at":"2026-05-27T21:02:18Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/390551d61d57ce68c2a80ed78c07eaa8e985908b","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/390551d61d57ce68c2a80ed78c07eaa8e985908b","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/390551d61d57ce68c2a80ed78c07eaa8e985908b/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"f87d61f01a23fcfb994e88b7f9324d404e66faef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f87d61f01a23fcfb994e88b7f9324d404e66faef","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f87d61f01a23fcfb994e88b7f9324d404e66faef"}]},{"sha":"f87d61f01a23fcfb994e88b7f9324d404e66faef","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKGY4N2Q2MWYwMWEyM2ZjZmI5OTRlODhiN2Y5MzI0ZDQwNGU2NmZhZWY","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-05-27T20:18:14Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-27T20:18:14Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): return grep errors for sandbox exec failures (#3637)\n\nFixes #3441\n\n---\n\n`SandboxBackend.grep` now treats non-zero backend `execute()` results as\ntool-level grep errors instead of attempting to parse backend\ndiagnostics as grep matches. The grep parser also uses NUL-delimited\nfilenames so paths containing `:` do not conflict with `path:line:text`\nparsing.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Callers that were relying on the previous `ValueError` crash for\nbackend exec failures will now receive `GrepResult(error=...,\nmatches=None)` instead.\n\n## Changes\n- Return `GrepResult(error=...)` when `BaseSandbox.grep` sees a non-zero\nbackend exec result, including a fallback `exit code N` message when the\nbackend provides no diagnostic output.\n- Parse grep output with NUL-delimited filenames via `grep -Z`,\npreserving support for filenames and matched text that contain colons.\n- Treat fully malformed zero-exit output as a structured grep error\nwhile keeping already parsed matches when later output lines are\nmalformed.\n- Preserve existing successful match parsing, empty-result behavior,\ndefault path handling, literal search, and `glob` include behavior.","tree":{"sha":"7dc1c78176f52a0b9517e6e0d8ff9f897685ce47","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/7dc1c78176f52a0b9517e6e0d8ff9f897685ce47"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/f87d61f01a23fcfb994e88b7f9324d404e66faef","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqF1GGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtq4QAG4BZi/6UpnzQPQ1OKtih4k9\nMUi/UCvzUqsb5UaPCXLujTRc+C2bvTCYLzobExs6iNaqu20DAQOypewEYuxGrfDS\nde8cYvJws6pkVi0WlIs5c5/PXtqEET9fImvQ1+PZW7LZZfCYQqkuD27wIXdHQJi8\niLkf4DO/1noZKd7cZTFxeGo1B/Ojc2TwfdJZMkAIbc5MifEVpYcZEQ1Ts+mxsJsE\n2n9nY5FS6x/YBRoS/PpjFIZfza/Hk3NCzd8xN2y4iT1SrzLufYMhFJUC8X8Y+Bix\niwVntkinadmEonc8W51U85U4RK+0iBWaviItznK2DABnV1z8AXM6kOoXWrWp3yIa\nA5I5eyReWMboY/FQxhd2DNdXJ1VdI0jb4RmVOZXvinGJc1MEgQ/bfgMzs8+kiY/m\ngJz9geQ3ppK54E/kiMW5ihqnY+KQxV569DgnPMVbBOqPJlNg3XhcysP3cr2LTjvd\nbFA8pymQ2Uz+raC1hYpGYWloKyhgtWdjO9OMWe9UQSJQK4yCUihfQ/m+dObv+RcO\nfN54a3miCQj4Fqbti8moUSkenb5gu6TvsIdgyldiPUBp6IyWn71JbGKIX0WULug5\nRaRaWzBPdsxwVf1K4cAB/2faAXH09H5co7MlCc7rxbhtaIZY9nPoxyRm9nc9jzic\nMTyv93PXbQ0qN1wPYOvW\n=mqZ5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 7dc1c78176f52a0b9517e6e0d8ff9f897685ce47\nparent 5a6d920d9dec2199cbe743062a5cc1ff8f298567\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1779913094 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779913094 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): return grep errors for sandbox exec failures (#3637)\n\nFixes #3441\n\n---\n\n`SandboxBackend.grep` now treats non-zero backend `execute()` results as\ntool-level grep errors instead of attempting to parse backend\ndiagnostics as grep matches. The grep parser also uses NUL-delimited\nfilenames so paths containing `:` do not conflict with `path:line:text`\nparsing.\n\n> [!WARNING]\n> Callers that were relying on the previous `ValueError` crash for\nbackend exec failures will now receive `GrepResult(error=...,\nmatches=None)` instead.\n\n## Changes\n- Return `GrepResult(error=...)` when `BaseSandbox.grep` sees a non-zero\nbackend exec result, including a fallback `exit code N` message when the\nbackend provides no diagnostic output.\n- Parse grep output with NUL-delimited filenames via `grep -Z`,\npreserving support for filenames and matched text that contain colons.\n- Treat fully malformed zero-exit output as a structured grep error\nwhile keeping already parsed matches when later output lines are\nmalformed.\n- Preserve existing successful match parsing, empty-result behavior,\ndefault path handling, literal search, and `glob` include behavior.","verified_at":"2026-05-27T20:18:15Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f87d61f01a23fcfb994e88b7f9324d404e66faef","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/f87d61f01a23fcfb994e88b7f9324d404e66faef","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/f87d61f01a23fcfb994e88b7f9324d404e66faef/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"5a6d920d9dec2199cbe743062a5cc1ff8f298567","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5a6d920d9dec2199cbe743062a5cc1ff8f298567","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5a6d920d9dec2199cbe743062a5cc1ff8f298567"}]},{"sha":"5a6d920d9dec2199cbe743062a5cc1ff8f298567","node_id":"C_kwDOPTymldoAKDVhNmQ5MjBkOWRlYzIxOTljYmU3NDMwNjJhNWNjMWZmOGYyOTg1Njc","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mason Daugherty","email":"mason@langchain.dev","date":"2026-05-27T19:50:34Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-05-27T19:50:34Z"},"message":"fix(sdk): handle `None` state in messages delta reducer (#3636)\n\nFixes #3564\n\n---\n\n`DeltaChannel.replay_writes` can pass `state=None` when a thread's\nearliest checkpoint never seeded `messages: []`. The reducer now treats\n`None` as an empty list, preventing `convert_to_messages` from receiving\na `None` argument. Regression tests for langchain-ai/deepagents#3564\nincluded.\n\n---\n\nNote: intentionally diverging from upstream, will port back later","tree":{"sha":"5dd893f0168183cb014011aa458c0dbef7e4d82f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/trees/5dd893f0168183cb014011aa458c0dbef7e4d82f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/git/commits/5a6d920d9dec2199cbe743062a5cc1ff8f298567","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqF0sKCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAATFAQAJMOaS6p3EDCgQzNAartvTiv\nVzVW+T6OSYEo0kwf4DhQx1q7hryN7TiDPkBzzvI1SVaNJkXOpBLuHeAdbQ/Gcxlc\ntHy5sz4Zx9dQtGsZNZGdtMzAPqBIC6xgqMwbTd+w1Efp9dowLGFrHd8sioPHJG0h\nNhI1qqiYZ73tq2bu8p8fOV3uljJR9ZanCBV6+1vhClkXJklVTZPB6nLo8KtXCWAS\nP7Yo8JcCqhZY1vj9sJtNPJBFrSyEvBlBFNdcltzCOivtp9FaotZ4zbBofSptAdnL\n5MJYcdPIvJ9gLwC8uzjeFJvDACXQToru7EtjaDZtKhBZvIVFrI+LTowavIEa1jQ6\niH78FkLESwTjXjTcxmL7sn4J4bCqW9IoiYGW3ETsSg2IISMvMgQfDvE+4S4ZiOTC\nP3qjdLHJi/V/6+TvV2uaTx7rT9f3NnkR1uDZreyHMtiXrsxvRZeL/7kO5K5ijdm2\nIB47yD9MHgbj9488NieX/BDDXr0mPqytwA8RBIETKCGzjY48b6f7yt/hbaY9RDLL\nSClYEdUME3+EWWe0Of89h/gQsoQRGT5/Xfuu9+kisEi8xbpYSTzgJD6FJr+CAeVv\n4lKOqTmhpiKYAqtUINisUTUUHlZLsv51WCl878ss3AuVm/m3EuLO4U96WQHWTm+u\nYrhnb454t74chquuWEan\n=VkVB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 5dd893f0168183cb014011aa458c0dbef7e4d82f\nparent e298206407e38a0d7bdb073d945b5ab19f401066\nauthor Mason Daugherty <mason@langchain.dev> 1779911434 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1779911434 -0400\n\nfix(sdk): handle `None` state in messages delta reducer (#3636)\n\nFixes #3564\n\n---\n\n`DeltaChannel.replay_writes` can pass `state=None` when a thread's\nearliest checkpoint never seeded `messages: []`. The reducer now treats\n`None` as an empty list, preventing `convert_to_messages` from receiving\na `None` argument. Regression tests for langchain-ai/deepagents#3564\nincluded.\n\n---\n\nNote: intentionally diverging from upstream, will port back later","verified_at":"2026-05-27T19:50:34Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5a6d920d9dec2199cbe743062a5cc1ff8f298567","html_url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/deepagents/commit/5a6d920d9dec2199cbe743062a5cc1ff8f298567","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/langchain-ai/deepagents/commits/5a6d920d9dec2199cbe743062a5cc1ff8f298567/comments","author":{"login":"mdrxy","id":61371264,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxMzcxMjY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61371264?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy","html_url":"https://github.com/mdrxy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mdrxy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"